    "result": "`solution.py` now implements both functions from `spec.md`, and `tests/test_solution.py` has 40 tests. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 40. I did not measure coverage, since the only command I'm allowed to run is the test command. By reading the code, every executable line of `solution.py` is exercised by at least one test, so I expect the 90% gate to pass.\n\n`can_book` checks the rules in the spec's order: it raises `ValueError` for `end <= start` or a negative buffer, then returns `False` for a booking that crosses midnight, lasts more than 4 hours, or falls outside opening hours. Conflicts are tested as half-open intervals with the buffer applied to both sides, so back-to-back bookings pass when the buffer is 0. `merge_intervals` validates every interval, sorts a copy by start, and merges overlapping or touching intervals, leaving the input unmodified. The tests cover the boundary cases the spec calls out: exactly 4 hours, opening and closing times, back-to-back bookings, buffer gaps on each side, and the `ValueError` paths.",
